// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Karma Houdini
// @category Karma Tropes / Audience Reactions
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Karma_Houdini
// @domain   Narrative
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): a villain justly deserving punishment ends the story with NONE of it — no
// comeuppance, no loss, sometimes outright rewarded; the bad karma simply never lands. The exact
// INVERSE of Karmic Death: where that trope closes the moral ledger (the manner of the death answers
// the manner of the sin, audience [+Satisfied], -- justice), Karma Houdini leaves it OPEN at the
// final curtain — the wrong stays unanswered. It rides the same reckoning that Karmic Death pays
// off — action_dynamics' &Strikes(kind=$sin), the blow whose kind would mirror the crime — but the
// recognition fires on that blow's ABSENCE: at [+Endgame] no such reckoning exists. That endgame-
// absence is the same shape as Foreshadowing's Red Herring (a pending thread that never pays off by
// [+Endgame]); here the unpaid thread is the villain's own moral debt. The author FRAMES the open
// ledger (rhetoric's Frames), and the house, denied its catharsis, reads INJUSTICE: audience
// [#Resentful], a touch on -- injustice — the dark mirror of Karmic Death's satisfied -- justice.
// Exaggerated: the villain is not merely spared but REWARDED. FRONTIER: a recognition keyed to a
// MISSING reckoning at [+Endgame] — the guilt is asserted, the karmic blow is not, and that gap IS
// the trope (the cutter walks; the drowner is never drowned).


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"               // justice, injustice, consequence, accountability, guilt
import "trl/modules/action_dynamics.trl"      // &Strikes(kind=$sin) — the reckoning that never comes
import "trl/modules/rhetoric.trl"             // Frames -> the author frames the open ledger; audience appraisal
import "trl/tropes/karmic_death.trl"          // the inverse: the ledger CLOSED, the blow mirroring the sin

// Lateral thematic links (optional, machine-followable — for discovery / embeddings).
assoc karma_houdini -> [
  karmic_death     : "inverse of",
  foreshadowing    : "shares the endgame-absence shape of a Red Herring with",
  action_dynamics  : "the &Strikes reckoning that never lands, of",
  rhetoric         : "the open ledger framed, appraised by the audience-engine of",
  injustice        : "the house reads",
  consequence      : "the sin's own, never returned",
  accountability   : "escaped entire",
  complicity       : "the story's silence reads as"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// The wrong that never pays — moral accounting left open at the final curtain.
imply KarmaHoudini -> [Impunity, Irony, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Recognition (the mirror of Karmic_Death): a villain is [+Guilty(of=$sin)] — the crime named by its
// kind — and the story reaches its [+Endgame] with NO reckoning of that sin: no &Strikes whose kind
// is $sin ever falls on them. The one bound $sin does the work it does in Karmic Death, but here it
// appears in the guilt and is ABSENT from any blow — the manner that WOULD mirror the wrong never
// arrives. That endgame-absence is the Red-Herring shape (a thread pending at the curtain); the unpaid
// thread is the villain's moral debt. The author FRAMES the open ledger, and the house — denied the
// catharsis Karmic Death grants — reads injustice: audience [#Resentful], a touch on -- injustice.
// The villain walks [+Triumphant], the debt unsettled: $villain !-- consequence, !-- accountability.
// That MISSING blow, not any blow, IS Karma Houdini (it tags the ending that let him go).
rule Karma_Houdini {
  when:
    char  $villain [+Guilty(of=$sin)]
    scene $endgame [+Endgame]
    evt   $f [&Frames(agent=author, target=$endgame, as=unanswered)]
    not ( evt $reckoning [&Strikes(target=$villain, kind=$sin)] )   // the karmic blow never falls
  then:
    $villain [+KarmaHoudini]
    $villain [+Triumphant]
    $villain !-- consequence
    $villain !-- accountability
    $endgame [+KarmaHoudini]
    audience [#Resentful]
    audience -- injustice
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: A Clockwork Orange — "I was cured all right" (novel/film, 1962/1971) ===
// Alex DeLarge leads his droogs through a spree of beatings, rape, and a killing, gleeful and
// remorseless. Caught, he is handed to the State's Ludovico Technique — conditioning that would make
// violence sicken him, the closest thing to a reckoning the story offers. But the cure is a political
// embarrassment, and the same State that imposed it REVERSES it to save face: the aversion is undone,
// Alex restored to exactly the predator he was, his public image rehabilitated in the bargain. The
// film closes on him unrepentant, untouched, free — "I was cured all right." No blow ever answers the
// crimes; the ledger stays open at the curtain. The guilt is asserted (the spree); the reckoning that
// would mirror it (a &Strikes for his cruelty) is exactly the event that never occurs — so the engine,
// at [+Endgame], finds the debt unpaid and names the ending Karma Houdini.

// ALEX DeLARGE — the droog whose violence the story never makes him answer for
char alex [+Antagonist]
alex [+Guilty(of=cruelty)]

// THE STATE — imposes the cure, then reverses it for its own convenience (its complicity is the edge below)
char the_state [+Authority]

// INT. THE HOSPITAL WARD — DAY (the reversal, the press, the offered post)
set hospital_ward [+Interior] [+Day]

// the final curtain falls here [+Endgame] — the scene at which the moral ledger is read, still open
scene the_reversal [+Endgame] {
  beat 1 {
    alex @ hospital_ward
    the_state @ hospital_ward
    // the State's crime is established: it undoes the only reckoning, for its own face
    the_state -- complicity : "reversed the cure to bury a scandal, freeing the predator"
  }
  beat 2 {
    // The author frames the final curtain as an OPEN ledger — the wrong left unanswered.
    evt closing_curtain [&Frames(agent=author, target=the_reversal, as=unanswered)]
        dialog(inject=[speaker=alex], inline="""
               speaker: "{speaker}"
               cue: "grinning into the vision of violence, conditioning peeled away, scot-free"
               tone: gleeful, unrepentant
               text: "I was cured all right."
               """)
    // Karma_Houdini fires: alex [+Guilty(of=cruelty)], the scene is [+Endgame], the author frames
    //   the ending unanswered, and NO &Strikes(target=alex, kind=cruelty) ever falls ->
    //   alex [+KarmaHoudini] [+Triumphant]; alex !-- consequence !-- accountability;
    //   audience [#Resentful]; audience -- injustice. The reckoning's ABSENCE is the trope.
  }
}
